    <!-- > Help & FAQ -->
    <string name="help_title">HELP &amp; FAQ</string>
    <string name="help_header_subtitle">Find answers to common issues and learn how to get the most out of the plugin.</string>
    <string name="help_q1">Why is the generated file empty or missing files?</string>
    <string name="help_a1">Check your filters. Make sure the extensions are in the \"Inclusions\" section, or verify that the maximum size limit isn\'t too low. Also, ensure .gitignore rules aren\'t excluding your code.</string>
    <string name="help_q2">How do I use this with ChatGPT or Claude?</string>
    <string name="help_a2">Tap \"Share file\" instead of \"Export\". Select your AI app (ChatGPT, Claude, etc.) from the share menu. You can then prompt the AI: \"Here is my project code, please review it...\".</string>
    <string name="help_q3">The Git section says it\'s not a repository.</string>
    <string name="help_a3">If you are inside a subfolder, tap the \"Go to project root\" action. Also, make sure the Git integration is enabled in CodeAssist\'s plugin settings.</string>
    <string name="help_q4">Where are the files saved?</string>
    <string name="help_a4">Exported files are saved in your device\'s storage under the path: Downloads/OneCodeForAI.</string>
    <string name="help_q5">Are binary files excluded automatically?</string>
    <string name="help_a5">Yes. Binary detection is enabled by default and can be turned off in the global preferences (Binaries section). When disabled, binary files are included as-is and may produce an unreadable dump.</string>
    <string name="help_q6">What does the maximum size mean?</string>
    <string name="help_a6">It is a per-file limit expressed in kilobytes. Files larger than the limit are skipped, not truncated. The value is remembered across sessions.</string>
    <string name="help_q7">Can I export a branch, tag, or commit?</string>
    <string name="help_a7">Yes, when the project is a Git repository. Open the reference picker from the dialog, choose a local or remote branch, a tag, or a recent commit, and preview the diff against the working tree before exporting.</string>
    <string name="help_q8">Can I reuse my filters across projects?</string>
    <string name="help_a8">Yes. Profiles store inclusions, exclusions, size limit, and the other filter properties. Built-in profiles cover Android/Kotlin, Web, Python, and plain text; custom profiles are persisted across launches.</string>
    <string name="help_q9">Will I lose my profiles or preferences after an update?</string>
    <string name="help_a9">No. Preference keys, JSON property names, and profile names are preserved across versions. Custom profiles and the last saved state remain available after installing a new APK.</string>
    <string name="help_q10">The plugin does not appear in CodeAssist. What do I do?</string>
    <string name="help_a10">Confirm that the plugin is enabled in the CodeAssist plugins section, then restart the host. If it still does not appear, verify that the installed build targets CodeAssist Plugin API 4.</string>
    
    <!-- values/strings.xml -->
    <string name="help_icon_description">Section help</string>
    <string name="help_inclusions_title">Inclusions</string>
    <string name="help_inclusions_body">Whitelist of extensions and glob patterns, evaluated before .gitignore.\n\nSupported syntax (same as .gitignore patterns):\n\u2022 Extensions: kt, json, xml\n\u2022 Wildcards: *.log, **/*.kt, src/*.kt\n\u2022 Directories: build/, **/generated/**\n\nAny file matching an inclusion is exported even if .gitignore or exclusions would skip it.\n\nInclusions take priority over exclusions and over .gitignore. Use it to force-include specific files or extensions.</string>
    <string name="help_exclusions_title">Exclusions</string>
    <string name="help_exclusions_body">Blacklist of extensions and glob patterns.\n\nSupported syntax (same as .gitignore patterns):\n\u2022 Extensions: log, tmp, pyc\n\u2022 Wildcards: *.log, **/*.test.kt, src/*.bak\n\u2022 Directories: build/, **/generated/**\n\nAny file matching an exclusion is skipped, even if .gitignore would include it. Inclusions take priority over exclusions.\n\nTo exclude a specific folder without writing a pattern, use the file tree below.</string>
    <string name="help_gitignore_title">Gitignore rules</string>
    <string name="help_gitignore_body">Rules detected in the project\'s .gitignore file.\n\nThis list is read-only \u2014 edit .gitignore directly to change it.\n\nInclusions and exclusions take priority over these rules: adding a matching inclusion or exclusion forces the file in or out regardless of .gitignore. Overridden rules are highlighted in amber.</string>
    
    
